  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 218 AM EST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\n=== Valley Fog This Morning ===\n\nLight winds and clear skies have allowed for efficient radiational \ncooling. Temperatures are in the mid 20s in the cold valley spots \nand low-mid 30s for most. Similar to the previous night, river \nvalley fog has developed. Will continue to monitor the extent of the \nfog, but an SPS may be needed in the next few hours for areas of \ndense fog and slick spots, given sub-freezing temperatures. \n\n=== Dry and Warming a Few Degrees Each Day This Week ===\n\nRidging will gradually move east and amplify. This will in turn \nintensify the surface high pressure centered over the Ohio Valley. \nBy Tuesday, this high pressure will reach a max intensity of about \n1036mb. Increasing heights/thicknesses and mostly sunny skies will \nallow temperatures to increase about 3-4 degrees each day. By the \nend of the week, we will see highs in the upper 60s and brushing the \nlow 70s in some spots. Mixing will allow for drier air to mix down \nto the surface each afternoon, placing afternoon RHs in the 28-35% \nrange. By the end of the week, high pressure should push off the the \neast as upper troughing approaches from the west. This will allow \nwinds to veer from the south, which may usher in warmer \ntemperatures. On Saturday, we may see temperatures overachieve in \nthe 70s. \n\n=== Small Chance for Rain on Sunday ===\n\nThe aforementioned troughing will bring a low pressure system \nthrough the Great lakes region on Sunday morning. As the cold front \nmoves through the lower Ohio Valley, there will be a chance for rain \nshowers. However, the antecedent dry airmass will attempt to squash \nany incoming moisture. It will likely be a battle between the two \nairmasses. Over the last few deterministic/ensemble runs, there has \nbeen consistency/confidence with location and timing of the low \npressure system, but inconsistency with rain chances. \n\nBehind this system, high pressure will bring dry conditions through \nthe beginning of next week.",
